Package: RAssistant
Title: A Lightweight AI Assistant for RStudio
Version: 0.16.4
Authors@R: person("MySimpleSmart", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "120612480+MySimpleSmart@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Opens the existing Source-aware chat assistant in the RStudio
    Viewer. Supports image uploads, optional live console context, contextual R help,
    a project Knowledge Base (PDFs, notes, R examples and custom instructions),
    reviewed Source edits and explicitly approved script validation. Stores optional credentials
    in the operating system credential store, separately from package updates.
License: file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2.0)
Imports:
    askpass,
    callr,
    commonmark,
    ellmer (>= 0.5.0),
    htmltools,
    httpuv,
    jsonlite,
    keyring (>= 1.3.0),
    knitr,
    later,
    remotes,
    rlang,
    rstudioapi,
    shiny (>= 1.14.0)
Suggests:
    httr2,
    pdftools
URL: https://github.com/MySimpleSmart/RAssistant
BugReports: https://github.com/MySimpleSmart/RAssistant/issues
Config/RAssistant/Changes: Automatically load the selected provider's model catalog when opening the picker, changing providers, or entering a key. Refresh models retries discovery without making a chat request.
    Show API-reported models separately from configured IDs absent from the latest catalog. Remove obsolete options before each lookup; keep the current model until the user explicitly selects Use model.
    Reject stale discovery responses after provider, endpoint or credential changes. Report discovery failures without presenting saved defaults as verified available models.
